In htsjdk, `SAMFileWriterFactory` can take a `SAMFileHeader` and write a text SAM file:
`new SAMFileWriterFactory().makeSAMWriter(reader.getFileHeader(), true, new File("/tmp/tumor.sam"))`!
And then:
`for (SAMRecord r : reader) writer.addAlignment(r); writer.close(); reader.close();`!
Once we have `/tmp/tumor.sam` and `/tmp/normal.sam` as text files, we can parse them in 100% pure Python!
Let's test this in JEXL right now!",
